                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>Computer Division is the IT services centre and is the backbone of the University for providing various computing and network services through Information & Communication Technologies (ICTs). The Division offers services to the Learners, Staff and Faculty at the Hqrs, Regional Centres, Study Centres, Partner Institutions across India and abroad. The Website of the University ‘www.ignou.ac.in’   is used for the extensive student support services in a virtual mode.</p>
</div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>Computer Division is the technology backbone of the University for providing various Computing and Network services through Information & Communication Technologies (ICTs). The Division offers IT services to the Learners, Staff and Faculty at the Headquarters New Delhi, Regional and Study Centres across India and also Partner Institutions in various Counties. The Website of the University ‘www.ignou.ac.in’ is a Learners’-centric digital interface of the University that facilitates Learners’ for various Online/Offline services during their learning life cycle that starts from Admission to the Convocationin virtual mode.</p>
<p>The Division also provides various ICTservices for e-Governance of the University that includes the HR, the Finance and Student Management. In addition, the Division develops Application Software, Website Interfacing, System & Network Administration, SAMARTH Project implementation, IT Infrastructure Procurement, Commissioning and Maintenance, e-Procurement (through CPP and  GeM), Training & Capacity Building and User Support</p></div>
